// Shared bias + exact ONNX PReLU epilogue of the hand-written srvgg conv
// kernels. srvgg_conv.comp (naive direct) and srvgg_conv_tiled.comp
// (shared-memory tiled) differ only in how they accumulate the conv sum; the
// tail that turns the raw accumulator into an activated output is identical.
//
// Factored as macros (not functions) and included textually with
// GL_GOOGLE_include_directive so the preprocessor expands the same tokens in
// both kernels: the generated SPIR-V carries the same instructions as the
// inlined originals, no extra OpFunction/OpFunctionCall. The bias is kept an
// expression (the naive kernel does `acc += bias`, the tiled kernel fuses it
// into `float acc = accs[i] + bias`) so neither kernel's structure changes.
// Requires the weights buffer `w_data`, the output channel `oc` and the
// push-constant block `p` in scope.
//
// Exact ONNX PReLU: x >= 0 ? x : slope * x (conv17: hasPrelu = 0).
#define SRVGG_CONV_BIAS(oc) (w_data[p.bBase + oc])
#define SRVGG_CONV_PRELU(acc, oc)     \
    if (p.hasPrelu == 1 && acc < 0.0) \
        acc *= w_data[p.sBase + oc];
